1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,527
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,837 --> 00:00:05,829
Hugo Strange can fix Butch.

3
00:00:06,039 --> 00:00:08,372
Strange might be
my only hope, Tabby.

4
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:11,202
But whatever happens
after I walk out that door,

5
00:00:11,778 --> 00:00:13,041
I care about you.

6
00:00:13,447 --> 00:00:14,642
And I always will.

7
00:00:14,882 --> 00:00:17,351
JEREMIAH: <i>Jerome
is dead. Long live me.</i>

8
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:20,720
Oh, my God!

9
00:00:20,821 --> 00:00:22,915
I have bombs planted
around this city.

10
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:24,834
GORDON: These are the buildings
Jeremiah's planning to demolish

11
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:25,985
with his bombs.

12
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:27,584
Once those buildings are blown,

13
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:28,694
they collapse and create

14
00:00:28,762 --> 00:00:30,322
the labyrinth from
the finished drawing.

15
00:00:30,797 --> 00:00:33,562
GORDON: <i>I have the locations
of every bomb Jeremiah planted.</i>

16
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:38,134
How did they beat you, huh?

17
00:00:38,205 --> 00:00:39,503
I'll have to start again.

18
00:00:39,573 --> 00:00:43,305
I had a vision of
Gotham in flames.

19
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:45,573
Together we can
make that happen.

20
00:00:45,679 --> 00:00:47,944
Now listen closely
to what you must do.

21
00:00:51,518 --> 00:00:52,518
Come on, Selina.

22
00:00:52,953 --> 00:00:53,953
(ALFRED GRUNTS)

23
00:00:55,522 --> 00:00:57,718
It's okay, it's okay.

24
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:00,383
Make way.

25
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,655
We'll do everything we can.

26
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:04,357
But the evacuation has us
dealing with a skeleton crew.

27
00:01:04,431 --> 00:01:05,431
Bruce...

28
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:08,502
Selina, you're at the hospital.
You're gonna be okay.

29
00:01:09,236 --> 00:01:10,534
Are you gonna leave me?

30
00:01:11,238 --> 00:01:14,072
No, I'm gonna be right here.

31
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:15,573
(VOICE BREAKING) Promise?

32
00:01:16,376 --> 00:01:17,708
I promise.

33
00:01:25,319 --> 00:01:26,787
(RATTLING)

34
00:01:34,294 --> 00:01:36,229
You know, I don't know
why I brought him here.

35
00:01:37,698 --> 00:01:39,530
I should've killed him
when I had the chance.

36
00:01:40,801 --> 00:01:42,133
You did the right thing, Alfred.

37
00:01:42,235 --> 00:01:45,603
You say that. You didn't
see what he did to Selina.

38
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:49,072
All right, I better
get to the hospital.

39
00:01:49,176 --> 00:01:50,667
I'll stop by when I can.

40
00:01:51,144 --> 00:01:52,339
Alfred.

41
00:01:54,014 --> 00:01:56,392
Couldn't have put a cap in that
psycho and done the world a favor?

42
00:01:56,416 --> 00:01:57,440
Where are we?

43
00:01:57,517 --> 00:01:59,418
Bomb squad's at the
last site on the map.

44
00:01:59,486 --> 00:02:01,264
After they disarm the bomb,
they're gonna put it in the warehouse

45
00:02:01,288 --> 00:02:02,347
with all the others.

46
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:05,893
Also, the Mayor called. He
wants to lift the evacuation order.

47
00:02:06,159 --> 00:02:07,804
Tell him we are not doing
anything until we have

48
00:02:07,828 --> 00:02:09,319
all the bombs locked away.

49
00:02:11,431 --> 00:02:12,922
Pardon me, Jim.

50
00:02:18,839 --> 00:02:20,205
Don't you all have work to do?

51
00:02:26,713 --> 00:02:27,772
What is it?

52
00:02:27,848 --> 00:02:30,647
I'd like to press charges
against Bruce Wayne's butler.

53
00:02:31,785 --> 00:02:33,515
I mean, just look at my face.

54
00:02:34,287 --> 00:02:35,516
I think you look great.

55
00:02:35,622 --> 00:02:38,592
And I'd like to
speak to Bruce again.

56
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:42,324
We couldn't really talk before
what with his girlfriend bleeding out

57
00:02:42,429 --> 00:02:43,488
all over him.

58
00:02:45,966 --> 00:02:48,197
You tried to prove you're
better than your brother.

59
00:02:49,202 --> 00:02:52,331
But I'm still here.
The city's still here.

60
00:02:52,406 --> 00:02:54,398
You're a failure, Jeremiah.

61
00:02:55,575 --> 00:02:57,806
Enjoy Arkham. Your brother did.

62
00:02:58,178 --> 00:03:00,079
Put him in the box. Get
him ready for transport.

63
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,180
Bring me Bruce Wayne

64
00:03:01,248 --> 00:03:02,968
and I'll tell you where
the other bombs are.

65
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:05,713
We have all your bombs.

66
00:03:05,819 --> 00:03:10,120
The maze bombs, yes.
I mean the other ones.

67
00:03:12,392 --> 00:03:16,887
Jim, as an engineer,
you expect systems to fail.

68
00:03:16,997 --> 00:03:19,330
So, you build in redundancies.

69
00:03:21,001 --> 00:03:23,334
And I am a very good engineer.

70
00:03:26,573 --> 00:03:27,939
- You're bluffing.
- Am I?

71
00:03:29,009 --> 00:03:31,911
How many lives are
you willing to bet?

72
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:36,179
You're right, you
know. I did fail.

73
00:03:37,084 --> 00:03:40,020
I didn't yet understand the
vision I was servicing, but,

74
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:45,085
I do now. My eyes are
open as will yours be.

75
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:53,567
When you realize I'm not
bluffing, bring me Bruce Wayne.

76
00:03:55,435 --> 00:03:59,736
And I'd like a coffee.
Black. Two sugars.

77
00:03:59,806 --> 00:04:01,604
(EKG FLATLINING)

78
00:04:01,708 --> 00:04:03,700
No heartbeat.

79
00:04:05,212 --> 00:04:07,613
Extraordinary.

80
00:04:08,215 --> 00:04:09,215
This better work.

81
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:14,515
The chemicals that turned
him into this beautiful specimen

82
00:04:14,855 --> 00:04:18,053
kept his organs
surprisingly well-preserved.

83
00:04:18,291 --> 00:04:21,557
Once we flush his
body with anti-toxins,

84
00:04:21,628 --> 00:04:25,156
we'll top him off with
some fresh blood.

85
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:30,560
And a quick jolt to the heart
will see him good as new.

86
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:39,144
You hear that?
You're gonna be cured.

87
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:41,244
- Yeah.
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)

88
00:04:44,451 --> 00:04:45,451
What?

89
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:47,880
When?

90
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:49,381
- What is it?
- (GASPS)

91
00:04:50,657 --> 00:04:52,626
Selina's been shot by
that lunatic Jeremiah.

92
00:04:52,726 --> 00:04:54,092
She's at Gotham General.

93
00:04:54,661 --> 00:04:56,129
I have to go. I'll be back.

94
00:04:56,263 --> 00:04:58,630
Of course. You go
check on the kid.

95
00:04:58,698 --> 00:05:02,135
What? No, she's in surgery.
I'm gonna kill Jeremiah.

96
00:05:02,269 --> 00:05:04,101
- (GUN COCKING)
- I'm coming with you.

97
00:05:04,171 --> 00:05:06,868
I don't advise that. The
procedure should not be interrupted.

98
00:05:07,007 --> 00:05:08,270
(GROANING)

99
00:05:08,341 --> 00:05:09,434
TABITHA: Stay.

100
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:14,306
I'll be here. Making sure
everything goes as planned.

101
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:19,478
I'm doing this for
Butch. Not for you.

102
00:05:22,589 --> 00:05:23,852
It's okay.

103
00:05:35,068 --> 00:05:36,969
Unfortunately,
there's no telling

104
00:05:37,037 --> 00:05:39,199
just how many battery
bombs Jeremiah produced.

105
00:05:39,406 --> 00:05:41,637
He was fanatically secretive
about his technology

106
00:05:41,708 --> 00:05:43,472
and Bruce trusted him, so...

107
00:05:43,977 --> 00:05:45,275
He's gotta be bluffing.

108
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:46,345
Yeah.

109
00:05:47,113 --> 00:05:48,638
Cap, Mayor's on the phone again.

110
00:05:48,715 --> 00:05:51,651
The evacuation stays in effect.
I will tell him when it's lifted.

111
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:55,018
LUCIUS: <i>You think
there are more bombs?</i>

112
00:05:55,555 --> 00:05:58,354
Up till now, Jeremiah's actions
sprang from the fear and hatred

113
00:05:58,425 --> 00:05:59,484
of his brother.

114
00:05:59,559 --> 00:06:02,529
Even his obsession with Bruce
is just a reflection of Jerome's.

115
00:06:04,231 --> 00:06:06,200
What did he mean when
he said he didn't understand

116
00:06:06,266 --> 00:06:07,598
the vision he was serving?

117
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:10,261
That his eyes had been opened.

118
00:06:12,072 --> 00:06:15,065
BURKE: <i>Perhaps the previous
mayor took orders from a police captain.</i>

119
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:17,541
- Captain Gordon...
- Jim Gordon is not the Mayor

120
00:06:17,644 --> 00:06:19,135
of Gotham, I am.

121
00:06:19,846 --> 00:06:23,681
The people need to know the
city is safe. I'm lifting the order.

122
00:06:26,253 --> 00:06:27,482
What are you looking at?

123
00:06:27,721 --> 00:06:30,748
There's a man on the building
across the street, staring at us.

124
00:06:30,857 --> 00:06:31,857
What?

125
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,028
(WHINING)

126
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:47,097
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

127
00:07:00,654 --> 00:07:03,453
How many bombs are
there? Where are they?

128
00:07:03,556 --> 00:07:05,718
I want to talk to Bruce Wayne.

129
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,229
Tell me where they
are, you son of a bitch.

130
00:07:09,296 --> 00:07:10,320
Who's helping you?

131
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:12,331
Bruce Wayne.

132
00:07:12,766 --> 00:07:13,766
(GORDON GRUNTS)

133
00:07:14,734 --> 00:07:16,112
You are never gonna
talk to Bruce Wayne.

134
00:07:16,136 --> 00:07:17,136
You hear me?

135
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:19,296
Then more people will die.

136
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,408
Well, you never were good at
holding on to what you care about,

137
00:07:23,476 --> 00:07:24,739
were you, James?

138
00:07:26,646 --> 00:07:29,480
Jim, we need you out here now!

139
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:35,247
(HUMMING SOFTLY)

140
00:07:44,331 --> 00:07:45,526
Can I help you?

141
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:49,763
Captain Gordon? Major Rodney
Harlan, Seventh Division, Fort Henry.

142
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:52,838
Major, I assume you're here
to help with the evacuation.

143
00:07:52,939 --> 00:07:54,499
If so, Detective
Bullock can coordinate.

144
00:07:54,607 --> 00:07:56,235
The Governor has
declared martial law.

145
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:59,507
Until this crisis is
resolved, I'm in charge here.

146
00:08:00,747 --> 00:08:01,976
Are you serious?

147
00:08:02,048 --> 00:08:03,380
Son, this is not
a pissing match.

148
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:06,715
I was sent here to restore
order in a chaotic situation.

149
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:09,456
Can I count on you?

150
00:08:11,624 --> 00:08:13,525
- Yes, sir.
- What do we got?

151
00:08:13,793 --> 00:08:16,490
Not much. Valeska
had a plan to knock down

152
00:08:16,596 --> 00:08:18,030
a number of buildings in Gotham.

153
00:08:18,465 --> 00:08:20,627
We recovered those bombs,
but he's stashed away more.

154
00:08:20,867 --> 00:08:22,927
Who's helping him?
Somebody's gotta be.

155
00:08:23,003 --> 00:08:25,472
It's unclear. We've
heard reports that

156
00:08:25,538 --> 00:08:26,972
his followers have
turned on him,

157
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,640
which would indicate
he has someone else.

158
00:08:29,209 --> 00:08:32,509
He would like to talk to Bruce
Wayne. That's clearly a trap.

159
00:08:32,612 --> 00:08:34,012
His brother pulled the same gag.

160
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,558
There was a blimp,
it was a whole thing.

161
00:08:35,582 --> 00:08:38,017
We'll make sure he's
safe. Get me Bruce Wayne.

162
00:08:38,084 --> 00:08:40,212
Major, you cannot bring
Bruce Wayne down...

163
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,720
Not your call, Captain.

164
00:08:42,589 --> 00:08:44,319
- Now.
- Yes, sir.

165
00:08:44,991 --> 00:08:46,235
You have no idea
who you're dealing with.

166
00:08:46,259 --> 00:08:47,352
Arrest Captain Gordon.

167
00:08:47,427 --> 00:08:48,725
(ALL MURMURING)

168
00:08:48,828 --> 00:08:51,195
Hey, are you out of
your freakin' mind?

169
00:08:51,264 --> 00:08:53,597
You listen to me. This city
is holding on by a thread.

170
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:56,192
I would not allow anything
to jeopardize it further.

171
00:08:56,269 --> 00:08:58,033
Including insubordination.

172
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:00,097
Escort Captain
Gordon across the river.

173
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:01,720
Hold him there till
you hear from me.

174
00:09:01,775 --> 00:09:03,107
Get me Bruce Wayne.

175
00:09:07,414 --> 00:09:09,576
(MUFFLED GUNSHOTS)

176
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:14,881
I strike where you lie.
Death's gentle cousin.

177
00:09:15,488 --> 00:09:17,184
The answer is sleep, Ed...

178
00:09:20,326 --> 00:09:21,919
It's polite to let
people finish.

179
00:09:32,672 --> 00:09:34,402
Rise and shine!

180
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:36,736
Good morning, sweetheart.

181
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:40,576
I know. Waking up in
the Narrows, a prisoner.

182
00:09:40,647 --> 00:09:42,309
Must feel like history
repeating itself.

183
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:43,439
Ed.

184
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:45,990
Speaking of history, remember
when you punched me in the face?

185
00:09:46,653 --> 00:09:47,780
(GRUNTING)

186
00:09:49,622 --> 00:09:50,783
That felt good.

187
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:57,292
Listen to me. Jeremiah
Valeska has more bombs.

188
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,657
- You have to...
- I have to what, Jim?

189
00:10:00,900 --> 00:10:03,563
Set you free?
Help save the city?

190
00:10:03,837 --> 00:10:06,534
Well, we've been there,
done that. And guess what?

191
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:09,735
Shocker! Lee and
I are still fugitives.

192
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:11,809
I offered her a way out.

193
00:10:11,911 --> 00:10:13,311
Oh, by returning the money?

194
00:10:13,413 --> 00:10:16,042
She's dispersed that among
all the deadbeats of the Narrows.

195
00:10:16,216 --> 00:10:17,878
Not exactly what I
would have done.

196
00:10:18,218 --> 00:10:21,985
But, point is, it's gone.
Now, on with the show.

197
00:10:22,088 --> 00:10:24,648
We're a little pressed for time.

198
00:10:25,158 --> 00:10:27,286
(NYGMA LAUGHING)

199
00:10:29,996 --> 00:10:31,396
Ed, Ed, Ed...

200
00:10:31,464 --> 00:10:35,492
Wait. Ed. Wait, wait, Ed.

201
00:10:35,602 --> 00:10:38,162
- This is 50 pounds of pressure.
- (GRUNTING)

202
00:10:39,172 --> 00:10:40,504
What are you doing?

203
00:10:41,107 --> 00:10:43,167
(IN FRENCH) <i>Peine forte et dure.</i>

204
00:10:43,943 --> 00:10:45,223
Was my own version of it anyway.

205
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:49,446
You see in the old days, they used
to pile weights on a prisoner's chest.

206
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:52,975
Tried to get a confession.
Usually, they just died.

207
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:55,015
- That's 100 pounds.
- (GROANING)

208
00:10:57,223 --> 00:10:58,223
Why?

209
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:01,826
To help Lee break
free from her history.

210
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:06,698
You see, she has this anchor,
deadweight holding her to her past,

211
00:11:06,799 --> 00:11:07,858
and that's you.

212
00:11:08,301 --> 00:11:11,430
Once you're gone, she'll
finally be free to be the person

213
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:12,972
she was meant to be.

214
00:11:13,039 --> 00:11:15,201
The person I want her to be.

215
00:11:15,308 --> 00:11:16,332
- (WHIRRING)
- (GROANING)

216
00:11:16,442 --> 00:11:18,377
- 150.
- (GRUNTING)

217
00:11:19,479 --> 00:11:23,439
You see, I saw you together. I
saw the way she looked at you.

218
00:11:23,783 --> 00:11:25,945
So, for her sake,
you're gonna die.

219
00:11:26,452 --> 00:11:30,150
And for my sake,
you're gonna suffer.

220
00:11:31,658 --> 00:11:33,058
(GRUNTING)

221
00:11:33,193 --> 00:11:34,957
Now, this is gonna
be so much fun.

222
00:11:35,228 --> 00:11:36,890
(LAUGHING)

223
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,331
This evacuation is going to
leave a lot of territory undefended.

224
00:11:43,736 --> 00:11:45,261
Shame not to capitalize.

225
00:11:47,774 --> 00:11:49,743
(GRUNTING)

226
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:53,740
Hello, Barbara.

227
00:11:56,249 --> 00:11:57,683
Was only hoping to talk.

228
00:11:57,750 --> 00:11:59,184
By attacking my people?

229
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:01,680
- Call it precaution.
- What do you want?

230
00:12:02,121 --> 00:12:06,081
I'm leaving Gotham and I
want you to come with me.

231
00:12:06,192 --> 00:12:08,093
(SCOFFS) Try again.

232
00:12:08,528 --> 00:12:12,829
I had a vision when I took
back the Demon's Head.

233
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:16,161
Death. Destruction.
The city in flames.

234
00:12:17,203 --> 00:12:18,203
But it didn't come to be.

235
00:12:18,605 --> 00:12:19,937
How disappointing for you.

236
00:12:20,039 --> 00:12:22,235
Indeed, for many reasons.

237
00:12:22,342 --> 00:12:25,437
Not least is that for centuries I
have depended on the Demon's head

238
00:12:25,545 --> 00:12:26,625
to get ahead of my enemies.

239
00:12:26,679 --> 00:12:29,012
But, without the full
measure of its power...

240
00:12:29,082 --> 00:12:33,281
Wait. Are you saying you think
some of it might still be in me?

241
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:39,355
Interesting. So I guess
you're here to kill me for it.

242
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:41,227
You misunderstand.

243
00:12:42,428 --> 00:12:45,421
Remember the woman from the
tapestry, the one whose features you share?

244
00:12:45,498 --> 00:12:47,967
The whore you murdered?
How could I forget?

245
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:50,828
I lied. To get under your skin.

246
00:12:52,772 --> 00:12:55,765
I loved her. Very much.

247
00:12:57,143 --> 00:13:00,238
I offered her eternity,
but she turned it down.

248
00:13:01,781 --> 00:13:04,341
And now, I make
you the same offer.

249
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:09,745
Join me. And we will rule the
League of Shadows together.

250
00:13:12,425 --> 00:13:13,586
Think about it.

251
00:13:17,430 --> 00:13:20,127
What about your
vision? The city on fire.

252
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:22,964
I am making certain
of it even now.

253
00:13:23,069 --> 00:13:26,062
Its destruction will give rise
to the one I foresaw long ago.

254
00:13:26,906 --> 00:13:30,274
The one who brought
me here, my heir.

255
00:13:36,683 --> 00:13:40,176
Bullock, can you tell this
putz to let us go, please?

256
00:13:40,286 --> 00:13:42,653
Major, the men escorting
Gordon were attacked.

257
00:13:42,955 --> 00:13:45,435
Your guys didn't see who. I'm
thinking it's either Valeska's...

258
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:47,722
Enough. Did you prepare
Valeska like I asked?

259
00:13:48,528 --> 00:13:49,655
Yeah.

260
00:13:50,363 --> 00:13:52,730
Mr. Wayne, you'll
be perfectly safe.

261
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:55,028
If you could help us learn
the location of the bombs...

262
00:13:55,134 --> 00:13:56,864
Major, you brought
me here against my will.

263
00:13:57,070 --> 00:13:59,699
I want to go back to the
hospital and back to my friend.

264
00:14:01,307 --> 00:14:02,400
Let's get this over with.

265
00:14:19,659 --> 00:14:20,683
Hello, Bruce.

266
00:14:22,295 --> 00:14:23,456
It's great to see you.

267
00:14:27,133 --> 00:14:28,829
Where are the bombs, Jeremiah?

268
00:14:28,901 --> 00:14:30,062
Closer, please.

269
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:36,732
Closer.

270
00:14:38,678 --> 00:14:42,740
Tell me. How is the
young lady doing?

271
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:53,759
You know why we're
destined to be best friends?

272
00:14:54,594 --> 00:14:58,361
Because we're very much
alike. You are as I used to be.

273
00:14:58,431 --> 00:15:00,195
At war with your true nature.

274
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:04,033
You must truly embrace it
if you ever want to be free.

275
00:15:04,103 --> 00:15:05,230
I'm just trying to help you.

276
00:15:06,539 --> 00:15:07,802
Trying to help me?

277
00:15:10,610 --> 00:15:11,976
By torturing Alfred?

278
00:15:13,713 --> 00:15:16,649
Trying to destroy Gotham?
By shooting Selina?

279
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:20,914
You think we're alike because
there's a darkness inside both of us.

280
00:15:21,254 --> 00:15:24,622
But the difference is, I
know how to control mine.

281
00:15:25,691 --> 00:15:28,525
I think you could be so strong.

282
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:31,022
I see it.

283
00:15:33,699 --> 00:15:34,962
He sees it too.

284
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:40,239
What do you mean, "he"?

285
00:15:43,309 --> 00:15:44,572
Ask him about the bombs.

286
00:15:46,112 --> 00:15:47,273
Where are the other bombs?

287
00:15:50,683 --> 00:15:52,174
What bombs?

288
00:15:53,586 --> 00:15:55,612
<i>Bombs you planted
around the city.</i>

289
00:15:55,822 --> 00:15:57,188
You blew up the Mayor.

290
00:15:57,824 --> 00:16:00,259
Ah, that bomb. Yes,
that was the only one.

291
00:16:00,326 --> 00:16:02,761
But it did what it had to do.

292
00:16:03,596 --> 00:16:04,757
It got you here.

293
00:16:06,499 --> 00:16:08,593
All right, that's enough.
I want my boy out, mate.

294
00:16:08,668 --> 00:16:10,762
- Mmm-mmm.
- You said, "he."

295
00:16:13,539 --> 00:16:15,007
Who do you mean?

296
00:16:15,174 --> 00:16:16,608
The one who opened up my eyes.

297
00:16:16,676 --> 00:16:18,668
Who showed me that
everything I was doing,

298
00:16:19,212 --> 00:16:21,272
was not to create a
Gotham of my own.

299
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:22,910
But yours.

300
00:16:23,950 --> 00:16:25,919
The Gotham you need.

301
00:16:26,452 --> 00:16:30,184
Your dark island. And
it will come to be, Bruce.

302
00:16:31,757 --> 00:16:32,850
Tonight.

303
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:37,095
Tell me his name.

304
00:16:37,163 --> 00:16:38,461
What did the doctors say?

305
00:16:38,531 --> 00:16:40,466
Will the little bitch
ever walk again?

306
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:42,461
What vertebrae did I sever?

307
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,269
I was hoping for the lumbar...

308
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:45,870
Tell me his name!

309
00:16:48,307 --> 00:16:51,368
You already know his
name. You're his heir.

310
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:54,507
Ra's al Ghul.

311
00:16:55,815 --> 00:16:57,147
- No, it can't...
- Shh.

312
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,042
(MAN SCREAMS)

313
00:17:00,152 --> 00:17:01,232
MAN: Bullock? HARVEY: Yeah.

314
00:17:14,534 --> 00:17:15,593
(WHIRRING)

315
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:20,002
- 350 pounds of pressure.
- (GRUNTS)

316
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:21,540
Getting hard to breathe?

317
00:17:21,607 --> 00:17:23,508
- (GRUNTS)
- I'll take that as a yes.

318
00:17:23,709 --> 00:17:27,305
You know, if we listen carefully,
we can hear some ribs cracking soon.

319
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:28,404
(LAUGHING)

320
00:17:28,514 --> 00:17:29,880
Four hundred fifty.

321
00:17:31,551 --> 00:17:35,352
Healthy male adult. His ribs should
be able to take about 450 pounds

322
00:17:35,421 --> 00:17:36,621
- before they crack.
- (GROANS)

323
00:17:39,425 --> 00:17:41,223
Do you think you could
hide this from me, Ed?

324
00:17:41,327 --> 00:17:43,887
I'm Queen of the Narrows.
People tell me things.

325
00:17:43,996 --> 00:17:45,020
I know how this looks.

326
00:17:45,097 --> 00:17:46,708
It looks like you're trying
to crush him to death

327
00:17:46,732 --> 00:17:48,932
because you think we still
have feelings for each other.

328
00:17:49,669 --> 00:17:52,730
Well, perhaps we should
jump to why this is a good thing.

329
00:17:52,838 --> 00:17:54,033
I can't wait.

330
00:17:54,206 --> 00:17:55,401
He's holding you back.

331
00:17:56,142 --> 00:17:57,201
From?

332
00:17:57,443 --> 00:18:01,539
From being the person
that you are meant to be.

333
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:04,273
The woman that I love.

334
00:18:05,985 --> 00:18:08,318
(SIGHS) You really
think so little of me?

335
00:18:09,589 --> 00:18:10,613
I don't follow that.

336
00:18:10,723 --> 00:18:13,989
How weak would that person need to
be if Jim Gordon could hold her back?

337
00:18:14,627 --> 00:18:15,627
It's actually insulting.

338
00:18:16,429 --> 00:18:17,954
That's not what I intended, I...

339
00:18:18,064 --> 00:18:19,088
Enough.

340
00:18:19,665 --> 00:18:24,069
Yesterday, you said a part of
you would always care for me.

341
00:18:24,437 --> 00:18:27,464
The woman you loved
is gone. Understand?

342
00:18:29,542 --> 00:18:30,601
Yes.

343
00:18:33,245 --> 00:18:35,942
The Narrows is free
from landlords and gangs.

344
00:18:36,382 --> 00:18:40,786
Every family has money to build
their life. I'm done. I'm leaving.

345
00:18:41,988 --> 00:18:45,481
I want you to come with me.
But if you kill Jim, don't bother.

346
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,991
And I will decide
who I'm going to be.

347
00:18:48,227 --> 00:18:51,220
Not you. Not Jim Gordon. Me.

348
00:18:52,098 --> 00:18:55,000
I'm leaving tonight.
It's your choice.

349
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,139
(DOOR CLOSES)

350
00:19:07,513 --> 00:19:08,879
She chose me, Jim.

351
00:19:11,317 --> 00:19:12,615
Did you hear that?

352
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,349
It's all I wanted.

353
00:19:17,623 --> 00:19:18,682
You can have Gotham.

354
00:19:24,563 --> 00:19:25,724
(GRUNTS)

355
00:19:26,365 --> 00:19:28,577
BARBARA: By the time I got
there, Jeremiah had already escaped.

356
00:19:28,601 --> 00:19:30,695
ALFRED: Right. Where
the hell is Ra's al Ghul?

357
00:19:30,803 --> 00:19:34,638
Alfred. Let me guess. Ra's
helped Jeremiah kidnap Bruce.

358
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,206
So you came to me to find Ra's.

359
00:19:36,642 --> 00:19:38,167
Would you care to
tell me where he is?

360
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:40,677
I don't know where he is. But
I know where he's gonna be.

361
00:19:41,447 --> 00:19:45,009
Ra's is leaving Gotham tonight
after turning it to a pile of rubble.

362
00:19:45,117 --> 00:19:47,313
With, I assume, Jeremiah's
help. So, here's the deal.

363
00:19:47,386 --> 00:19:50,379
You get to kill Jeremiah,
you get to rescue Bruce,

364
00:19:50,489 --> 00:19:52,151
and I get to kill Ra's.

365
00:19:52,558 --> 00:19:54,078
And how do you plan
on doing that then?

366
00:19:56,362 --> 00:19:57,830
I got a little surprise for him.

367
00:19:57,897 --> 00:19:59,195
PENGUIN: One question.

368
00:20:01,834 --> 00:20:03,325
Who do I get to kill?

369
00:20:05,404 --> 00:20:06,997
The only way to keep
Butch on the table

370
00:20:07,073 --> 00:20:08,735
was to promise I
would come help.

371
00:20:09,241 --> 00:20:10,436
Well.

372
00:20:11,777 --> 00:20:13,939
Don't we make
quite the little gang?

373
00:20:15,915 --> 00:20:17,213
Let's do this.

374
00:20:21,554 --> 00:20:23,113
- (GROANING)
- (SIREN WAILING)

375
00:20:26,125 --> 00:20:27,252
Hey.

376
00:20:29,829 --> 00:20:31,195
My car's around the corner.

377
00:20:32,364 --> 00:20:34,026
You're gonna
wanna ice those ribs.

378
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:37,203
Is it true about you
leaving Gotham?

379
00:20:37,870 --> 00:20:39,498
- Yes.
- And taking Ed with you?

380
00:20:40,106 --> 00:20:41,540
That's none of your concern.

381
00:20:43,843 --> 00:20:45,072
Back in the GCPD,

382
00:20:45,177 --> 00:20:47,544
when I told you there was
so much I wish I could change,

383
00:20:47,613 --> 00:20:49,206
- you asked me what I meant.
- Jim.

384
00:20:49,281 --> 00:20:51,841
I would change everything
that brought us to this point.

385
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:56,780
I would ask you to leave Gotham
with me that first moment I saw you

386
00:20:56,889 --> 00:20:58,649
and I would make sure
we had a life together.

387
00:21:00,526 --> 00:21:01,755
Then you wouldn't be you.

388
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:04,226
Maybe that'd be a good thing.

389
00:21:05,731 --> 00:21:06,926
No, it wouldn't.

390
00:21:10,069 --> 00:21:11,970
I'm not going back to who I was.

391
00:21:12,838 --> 00:21:16,400
But, what you said yesterday about
part of you always caring for me,

392
00:21:17,343 --> 00:21:18,504
I feel the same way.

393
00:21:25,751 --> 00:21:28,949
Goodbye. Now, go save Gotham.

394
00:21:35,594 --> 00:21:37,756
Ready at your command, Major.

395
00:21:37,830 --> 00:21:39,162
- Jim.
<i>- Harvey.</i>

396
00:21:39,265 --> 00:21:41,305
Thank God, you're all right.
What the hell happened?

397
00:21:41,333 --> 00:21:43,564
<i>It's a long story. Did Harlan
get Bruce to the precinct?</i>

398
00:21:43,636 --> 00:21:45,070
Yeah, it's bad.

399
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:46,581
<i>- What are you talking about?</i>
- (SIGHS)

400
00:21:46,605 --> 00:21:50,337
Jeremiah escaped. He's got
Bruce. He took the bombs, all of them.

401
00:22:11,230 --> 00:22:12,493
It's true.

402
00:22:13,632 --> 00:22:15,396
- How did you two...
- Find each other?

403
00:22:17,670 --> 00:22:19,536
I'd like to think it
was you, Bruce.

404
00:22:20,573 --> 00:22:22,804
You brought us together.

405
00:22:23,709 --> 00:22:25,200
I trust things went smoothly?

406
00:22:25,711 --> 00:22:26,838
Like clockwork.

407
00:22:29,481 --> 00:22:31,177
Did your men retrieve my bombs?

408
00:22:31,650 --> 00:22:35,314
They are en route to their
positions as we speak.

409
00:22:36,989 --> 00:22:38,116
From here,

410
00:22:39,158 --> 00:22:43,528
we can take in the full
majesty of Gotham's destruction.

411
00:22:47,399 --> 00:22:48,697
You're both insane.

412
00:22:49,301 --> 00:22:52,328
I know it's difficult
to fathom, Bruce.

413
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:56,740
But Jeremiah and I are
doing this for your benefit.

414
00:22:57,476 --> 00:22:59,741
How is destroying Gotham
supposed to help me?

415
00:22:59,912 --> 00:23:01,676
Because I had a vision.

416
00:23:01,747 --> 00:23:04,842
That out of this
crucible of blood and fire

417
00:23:04,917 --> 00:23:08,786
will rise the Dark Knight that
your city needs. That I need.

418
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:11,751
To be honest, Bruce.

419
00:23:12,858 --> 00:23:16,954
Prophesies, visions.
Not really my cup of tea.

420
00:23:19,031 --> 00:23:21,193
But our friend revealed
something to me.

421
00:23:22,635 --> 00:23:26,538
That my twin obsessions,
rebuilding Gotham and rebuilding you,

422
00:23:26,639 --> 00:23:28,699
are one and the same.

423
00:23:29,208 --> 00:23:30,767
You're the brother I never had.

424
00:23:33,445 --> 00:23:35,107
The one Jerome never could be.

425
00:23:36,749 --> 00:23:39,082
We will create a
legacy in this city.

426
00:23:40,185 --> 00:23:42,916
Gotham falls. We rise.

427
00:23:45,424 --> 00:23:46,585
Together.

428
00:23:52,231 --> 00:23:55,963
A dozen transport vans were
stolen from the GCPD motor pool.

429
00:23:56,568 --> 00:23:58,537
That's gotta be how
they're carrying the bombs.

430
00:23:58,604 --> 00:24:00,971
There were sightings
here, here and here.

431
00:24:01,073 --> 00:24:02,974
They're moving towards
the outskirts of Gotham.

432
00:24:03,075 --> 00:24:04,771
Jeremiah must have
changed targets.

433
00:24:04,877 --> 00:24:06,072
- Gordon.
- Perfect.

434
00:24:06,145 --> 00:24:08,808
You have some explaining to
do. What happened to my men?

435
00:24:08,914 --> 00:24:10,439
Major, we got
serious fish to fry...

436
00:24:10,516 --> 00:24:11,927
I didn't ask for your
opinion, Detective.

437
00:24:11,951 --> 00:24:13,471
Two more sightings.
Bolyston and Third,

438
00:24:13,519 --> 00:24:15,559
and they're moving north
along the Van Hook Highway.

439
00:24:15,587 --> 00:24:16,850
That doesn't make any sense.

440
00:24:16,956 --> 00:24:18,636
What buildings would
he be targeting there?

441
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:22,489
Told me Jeremiah promised to
turn Gotham into a dark island.

442
00:24:24,263 --> 00:24:27,165
We need to cancel the evacuation.
Get those people off the bridges.

443
00:24:27,266 --> 00:24:28,598
Absolutely not.

444
00:24:28,667 --> 00:24:30,145
They're filled with
people leaving the city.

445
00:24:30,169 --> 00:24:32,089
We bring them back into
Gotham. Buildings fall...

446
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:34,834
The bridges are the targets.
Harper, spread the word.

447
00:24:34,940 --> 00:24:37,205
Don't move. Arrest
Captain Gordon.

448
00:24:39,445 --> 00:24:40,674
I wouldn't do that.

449
00:24:41,747 --> 00:24:43,079
Arrest them both.

450
00:24:51,323 --> 00:24:52,757
Officer, your radio.

451
00:24:56,195 --> 00:24:59,791
This is Captain Gordon. I want
all the bridges cleared immediately.

452
00:24:59,932 --> 00:25:02,424
I repeat. Clear all the bridges.

453
00:25:03,669 --> 00:25:06,833
Civilization, so fragile, Bruce.

454
00:25:07,439 --> 00:25:11,809
Gotham is soon to be each man
for himself, a more savage place.

455
00:25:13,212 --> 00:25:14,373
Sounds like fun.

456
00:25:15,881 --> 00:25:17,144
Sure you wanna leave?

457
00:25:18,317 --> 00:25:20,252
Oh, hey, Bruce. Freak.

458
00:25:21,987 --> 00:25:25,480
Hello, Barbara. I'm
really glad you came.

459
00:25:26,825 --> 00:25:29,260
(SIGHS) Bad news,
baby. I'm not leaving.

460
00:25:29,828 --> 00:25:35,426
Gotham's in my blood. And I
don't think I can let you leave either.

461
00:25:36,702 --> 00:25:38,864
You re-forged it. Well now.

462
00:25:39,071 --> 00:25:41,631
You see, you say you're leaving.

463
00:25:41,707 --> 00:25:43,869
But I've got a feeling
you're gonna be back.

464
00:25:47,246 --> 00:25:49,477
And I don't like looking
over my shoulder.

465
00:25:50,015 --> 00:25:52,575
Need I remind you,
Barbara. You've already tried

466
00:25:52,684 --> 00:25:53,811
using that knife.

467
00:25:54,653 --> 00:25:57,680
And also, you're outnumbered.

468
00:25:58,223 --> 00:25:59,223
Hmm.

469
00:25:59,591 --> 00:26:01,924
That Demon's Head is really
not working out for you, huh?

470
00:26:05,597 --> 00:26:07,327
(PENGUIN SCREAMING)

471
00:26:10,702 --> 00:26:12,542
- (INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)
- (SIRENS WAILING)

472
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:20,805
Bullock, the hell is going on?
Why are we clearing the bridges?

473
00:26:20,913 --> 00:26:23,041
Because we said to
do it. Now, just do it.

474
00:26:23,115 --> 00:26:25,584
Did a GCPD transport
van come through here?

475
00:26:25,651 --> 00:26:26,795
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)
- About 20 minutes ago.

476
00:26:26,819 --> 00:26:27,819
Had to make way for it.

477
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:29,144
What's the status?

478
00:26:29,288 --> 00:26:30,732
HARPER: <i>All the
bridges are being cleared.</i>

479
00:26:30,756 --> 00:26:33,954
But I just heard from our choppers,
they've spotted vans on every bridge.

480
00:26:35,894 --> 00:26:39,092
The vans are in position.
Bombs could go off any minute.

481
00:26:41,133 --> 00:26:42,294
What the hell.

482
00:26:42,968 --> 00:26:44,027
HARVEY: Jim.

483
00:26:44,103 --> 00:26:45,264
GORDON: Out of the way.

484
00:26:45,938 --> 00:26:46,938
(GRUNTING)

485
00:26:53,912 --> 00:26:56,352
When will you ever learn,
Barbara? The knife has to be held...

486
00:26:56,415 --> 00:26:58,111
Held by Bruce Wayne. I get it.

487
00:26:58,250 --> 00:26:59,582
(BOTH GRUNTING)

488
00:27:05,991 --> 00:27:06,991
(ROPE TIGHTENING)

489
00:27:07,092 --> 00:27:09,254
So you know, this is for Selina.

490
00:27:09,394 --> 00:27:10,394
(GRUNTS)

491
00:27:14,066 --> 00:27:15,591
In that case,

492
00:27:16,001 --> 00:27:20,496
it must be very disappointing
for you to be dying like this.

493
00:27:21,106 --> 00:27:22,870
(GUNSHOTS)

494
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:38,650
What are you doing?

495
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:51,197
Well done, Barbara.

496
00:27:59,111 --> 00:28:02,138
(CAR ALARMS BLARING)

497
00:28:05,017 --> 00:28:07,350
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

498
00:28:31,543 --> 00:28:36,106
The choice is now
yours. Stay Bruce Wayne.

499
00:28:36,882 --> 00:28:41,616
Or accept your destiny.
Become Gotham's Dark Knight.

500
00:28:44,556 --> 00:28:45,922
(SCREAMING)

501
00:28:46,692 --> 00:28:47,692
(DAGGER CLATTERS)

502
00:29:08,013 --> 00:29:09,013
(EXHALES)

503
00:29:11,883 --> 00:29:14,079
Seems Jeremiah's
made good on his threat.

504
00:29:15,687 --> 00:29:17,451
And I take it that
means you're not leaving.

505
00:29:18,857 --> 00:29:20,120
How can I?

506
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:25,324
They need me more than ever
now. No one will help them but me.

507
00:29:28,734 --> 00:29:30,134
So, what does that mean for us?

508
00:29:33,338 --> 00:29:35,739
Ed, this is the end
of the road for us.

509
00:29:39,978 --> 00:29:42,846
All this time I've been
calling the other Ed stupid.

510
00:29:42,948 --> 00:29:44,348
And I'm the idiot.

511
00:29:48,954 --> 00:29:50,752
You were never
gonna leave with me.

512
00:29:52,591 --> 00:29:54,651
You just wanted
to save Jim Gordon.

513
00:29:56,762 --> 00:29:58,924
You and Jim really
aren't that different.

514
00:29:59,631 --> 00:30:01,122
You both think you know me.

515
00:30:02,100 --> 00:30:03,762
You both wanna change me.

516
00:30:04,736 --> 00:30:06,227
Neither one of
you really sees me.

517
00:30:06,305 --> 00:30:07,773
(GASPS)

518
00:30:12,678 --> 00:30:14,340
(GASPING)

519
00:30:15,147 --> 00:30:18,777
For what it's worth, Ed, I was
offering you something real.

520
00:30:21,620 --> 00:30:23,452
But I was never going
to be who you wanted.

521
00:30:24,623 --> 00:30:26,524
Sooner or later, you
were just gonna kill me.

522
00:30:26,625 --> 00:30:28,321
It's just what you do.

523
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:31,186
That's quite possible.

524
00:30:31,330 --> 00:30:32,730
(GRUNTS)

525
00:30:38,070 --> 00:30:39,504
But you're wrong, Lee.

526
00:30:39,971 --> 00:30:41,735
(BOTH GASPING)

527
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:43,069
I do see you.

528
00:30:53,552 --> 00:30:55,487
(BOTH GRUNTING)

529
00:31:11,970 --> 00:31:12,970
(GASPS)

530
00:31:14,239 --> 00:31:15,537
Calm.

531
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:18,576
Where is Butch? What
did you do with him?

532
00:31:20,645 --> 00:31:21,874
I'm right here.

533
00:31:33,959 --> 00:31:35,222
You're you.

534
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:38,625
Yeah. I'm me again.

535
00:31:41,967 --> 00:31:43,697
- Yeah.
- I love you.

536
00:31:47,773 --> 00:31:49,241
I love you too, baby.

537
00:31:55,947 --> 00:31:57,245
(CHUCKLES)

538
00:32:00,452 --> 00:32:01,715
Oswald,

539
00:32:04,089 --> 00:32:05,250
I'll never forget this.

540
00:32:06,558 --> 00:32:08,925
Anything you need, I'm there.

541
00:32:09,961 --> 00:32:11,020
Thank you, Butch.

542
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:16,201
I want you to know I
consider you a friend.

543
00:32:18,737 --> 00:32:20,467
And that I'm truly sorry.

544
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:22,606
What?

545
00:32:29,448 --> 00:32:31,314
(GROANING)

546
00:32:41,259 --> 00:32:43,956
Did you think I forgot that
you murdered my mother?

547
00:32:46,298 --> 00:32:48,460
That I just got over it?

548
00:32:50,769 --> 00:32:53,830
I have lived with
that pain every day.

549
00:32:54,639 --> 00:32:57,666
I could've killed you
any time I wanted,

550
00:32:58,009 --> 00:33:00,808
but I believe in
an eye for an eye.

551
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:03,812
You took away the
one person I loved,

552
00:33:03,915 --> 00:33:06,077
so I took away the
one person you loved.

553
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:09,587
And you get to live with that.

554
00:33:10,155 --> 00:33:11,487
(SCREAMING)

555
00:33:12,123 --> 00:33:13,785
(GRUNTING)

556
00:33:19,197 --> 00:33:20,426
All of this...

557
00:33:22,100 --> 00:33:23,966
Finding Strange, curing Butch,

558
00:33:24,970 --> 00:33:26,939
was all so you could
kill him in front of me?

559
00:33:29,174 --> 00:33:32,144
Exactly. But don't worry.

560
00:33:33,144 --> 00:33:35,909
In time, when I feel that
you have suffered enough,

561
00:33:37,716 --> 00:33:39,514
I will kill you too.

562
00:33:41,820 --> 00:33:43,914
Not if I kill you first.

563
00:33:46,892 --> 00:33:48,019
You're welcome to try.

564
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:51,862
(GRUNTS)

565
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:56,764
(SCREAMS) I'll kill you!

566
00:34:06,912 --> 00:34:07,971
BRUCE: Selina.

567
00:34:10,148 --> 00:34:11,148
How is she?

568
00:34:11,316 --> 00:34:12,316
She did well in surgery.

569
00:34:12,384 --> 00:34:14,250
But the bullet severed
her spinal cord.

570
00:34:14,352 --> 00:34:15,843
And the damage
is likely permanent.

571
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:19,752
Mr. Wayne, the
hospital is shutting down.

572
00:34:19,858 --> 00:34:21,053
This is the last ambulance

573
00:34:21,159 --> 00:34:24,493
leaving for the post. We have
room for you, but we need to go.

574
00:34:39,544 --> 00:34:40,637
Bruce.

575
00:34:44,149 --> 00:34:45,447
I can't leave, Alfred.

576
00:34:47,485 --> 00:34:48,714
Ra's was right.

577
00:34:49,621 --> 00:34:51,112
This is what I'm meant to do.

578
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:54,586
The city's abandoned,
Master Bruce.

579
00:34:54,659 --> 00:34:55,903
There's nothing more
you can do here, mate...

580
00:34:55,927 --> 00:34:57,054
Jeremiah is still out there.

581
00:34:57,128 --> 00:34:59,222
He is not your responsibility.

582
00:35:01,333 --> 00:35:03,962
Gotham is not
your responsibility.

583
00:35:08,139 --> 00:35:09,539
I'm making it mine.

584
00:35:13,645 --> 00:35:14,645
Um...

585
00:35:16,047 --> 00:35:17,481
Oh, sod it.

586
00:35:19,784 --> 00:35:20,877
All right, fine.

587
00:35:22,220 --> 00:35:23,620
- We'll both stay.
- No.

588
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:29,260
I need to know
Selina's gonna be okay.

589
00:35:31,563 --> 00:35:32,656
Please.

590
00:35:36,334 --> 00:35:37,334
(SIGHS)

591
00:35:38,770 --> 00:35:40,796
All right, I'll see
that she's safe.

592
00:35:42,807 --> 00:35:45,038
And then I'll come
back and I will find you.

593
00:35:48,146 --> 00:35:49,307
I promise.

594
00:36:03,495 --> 00:36:05,259
(ENGINE STARTS)

595
00:36:22,380 --> 00:36:24,815
HARVEY: You just can't throw
in the towel on an entire city.

596
00:36:24,883 --> 00:36:27,318
There's no way to know how
many bombs are still out there.

597
00:36:27,385 --> 00:36:29,445
The power's out, water
supply is damaged.

598
00:36:29,521 --> 00:36:31,319
You're giving up.
Plain and simple.

599
00:36:31,456 --> 00:36:35,188
We're proceeding with the
evacuation. Boats will run all night.

600
00:36:35,293 --> 00:36:38,263
Everyone leaves,
including the police.

601
00:36:38,363 --> 00:36:40,341
Now the Governor's
declared the city off-limits until

602
00:36:40,365 --> 00:36:41,833
this situation can be evaluated.

603
00:36:41,900 --> 00:36:42,900
I'm not leaving.

604
00:36:43,001 --> 00:36:44,697
So, if you're gonna
arrest me, do it now.

605
00:36:47,739 --> 00:36:48,739
(SIGHS)

606
00:36:51,943 --> 00:36:53,070
He's right, Jim.

607
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:56,037
Governor's given up on the place,
there's gonna be nobody here.

608
00:36:56,114 --> 00:36:57,582
Gangs are carving up turf.

609
00:36:58,049 --> 00:37:00,211
Two hours, this city's
gonna be a battleground.

610
00:37:07,559 --> 00:37:10,085
Hey, what are you
guys doing here?

611
00:37:14,499 --> 00:37:18,095
Yes, this will do nicely.

612
00:37:18,937 --> 00:37:21,236
This is our
territory. You can't...

613
00:37:28,580 --> 00:37:29,912
Now it's mine.

614
00:37:32,717 --> 00:37:35,846
I want a ring of fire.
Ten blocks wide.

615
00:37:36,888 --> 00:37:40,825
If anyone stands in
your way, burn them!

616
00:37:43,728 --> 00:37:44,728
(LAUGHS)

617
00:37:51,803 --> 00:37:52,964
The hell?

618
00:37:54,572 --> 00:37:56,768
No, not hell.

619
00:37:59,077 --> 00:38:00,077
(SCREAMING)

620
00:38:10,622 --> 00:38:13,057
Hell is what's coming.

621
00:38:14,659 --> 00:38:16,423
Penguin says fix them.

622
00:38:32,110 --> 00:38:35,774
What should I do with you?

623
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:42,518
Ra's al Ghul is gone.
You defeated him.

624
00:38:44,189 --> 00:38:47,785
We have spoken and
agreed. We will follow you.

625
00:38:53,398 --> 00:38:55,731
Wow, I am honored.

626
00:38:56,901 --> 00:38:58,392
(TABITHA GRUNTING)

627
00:39:00,238 --> 00:39:02,833
Tabitha. What happened?

628
00:39:02,907 --> 00:39:05,900
Penguin. He shot
me and killed Butch.

629
00:39:11,482 --> 00:39:14,714
Everything that is
wrong with Gotham,

630
00:39:15,386 --> 00:39:20,984
all the greed, the pain, the
corruption, the destruction,

631
00:39:21,059 --> 00:39:26,054
it can all be traced back
to one problem, men.

632
00:39:28,032 --> 00:39:33,369
Well, I think it is time we had
a men-free zone, starting here.

633
00:39:36,741 --> 00:39:39,836
(MEN SCREAMING)

634
00:39:58,529 --> 00:40:01,021
LUCIUS: That's better.
Much, much better.

635
00:40:02,267 --> 00:40:03,530
Lucius?

636
00:40:04,769 --> 00:40:07,068
I requisitioned one of
Jeremiah's battery bombs

637
00:40:07,138 --> 00:40:08,436
before it went to the warehouse.

638
00:40:08,539 --> 00:40:10,701
Just restored it to
its original purpose.

639
00:40:10,775 --> 00:40:12,801
It is an ingenious mechanism.

640
00:40:13,745 --> 00:40:15,270
I told him we were staying.

641
00:40:15,847 --> 00:40:19,682
Figured we could use some
help with the, uh, science stuff.

642
00:40:20,551 --> 00:40:22,042
And there are
others on their way.

643
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:24,715
This is our city. You're
going to need our help.

644
00:40:26,190 --> 00:40:29,888
Speaking of, there's
something I need you to do.

645
00:40:30,695 --> 00:40:32,254
(GRUNTING)

646
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:44,298
Where's Jeremiah?

647
00:40:44,409 --> 00:40:45,570
I don't know!

648
00:40:45,910 --> 00:40:48,641
You see him, you tell
him I'm looking for him.

649
00:41:12,537 --> 00:41:13,537
Bruce.

650
00:41:16,307 --> 00:41:18,071
You're not supposed to be here.

651
00:41:18,142 --> 00:41:19,303
Neither are you.

652
00:41:20,111 --> 00:41:21,773
There's a dozen cops downstairs.

653
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:24,510
You stayed to
fight for the city.

654
00:41:28,953 --> 00:41:31,422
The gangs are carving up
territory. We're gonna have to go

655
00:41:31,489 --> 00:41:32,650
block by block.

656
00:41:33,658 --> 00:41:36,093
I have no idea what
we're gonna find.

657
00:41:37,195 --> 00:41:40,495
A thing like this brings out
whatever's lurking in the shadows.

658
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:55,345
(SQUEAKING)

659
00:41:58,983 --> 00:42:00,007
(SCREAMING)

660
00:42:22,974 --> 00:42:24,169
The light.

661
00:42:25,977 --> 00:42:28,537
You're basically daring whatever
is out there to come after you.

662
00:42:30,214 --> 00:42:31,546
Let them come.

663
00:42:33,551 --> 00:42:35,577
There are still good
people out there.

664
00:42:37,722 --> 00:42:42,160
They need to know
we're here, willing to fight.

665
00:42:46,397 --> 00:42:48,059
I remember the night we met.

666
00:42:52,770 --> 00:42:54,762
You told me the
world may seem dark.

667
00:42:57,742 --> 00:42:59,074
But there is light.

668
00:43:46,891 --> 00:43:47,891
English - SDH
